factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 9 problems
  reel_script states the quarry application was for a 4-acre area in the article's sentence about the site, but the article's 4-acre figure is correct; however the reel_script says 'கடந்த 2021, 2023 மற்றும் 2026ஆம் ஆண்டுகளில் நடந்த கிராம சபைக் கூட்டங்களில்' which matches the article, so no issue there; the reel_script omits that the officials' inspection was done by revenue officials and surveyors without any prior notice being the cause of tension, which is covered, but it omits that the quarry was to be sub-divided per the notice sent to residents
  reel_script says the people 'எச்சரித்துள்ளனர்' that they will hold continuous protest and road blockade, which matches the article, but the reel_script says the people are 'கடும் எதிர்ப்பு' which is an embellishment of the article's 'எதிர்ப்பு' wording
  slides_spec slide 1 says the quarry is at 'சொக்கனூர் ஊராட்சி, சங்கராயபுரம் பிரிவு அருகே புதிய' with the line cut mid-phrase so the sentence 'புதிய தனியார் இடத்தில்' is ungrammatical and has no clear meaning in Tamil
  slides_spec slide 2 'முறையான அறிவிப்பு, கருத்துக் கேட்பு இல்லை என மக்கள்' is an ungrammatical fragment with no clear verb
  slides_spec slide 3 line 'குவாரி அனுமதியை மாவட்ட நிர்வாகம் கைவிட வேண்டும்' is placed after the '2021, 2023, 2026 கிராம சபைகளில் குவாரிக்கு' line, mixing two different facts into one slide sequence and leaving the first line ungrammatical
  slides_spec slide 3 line '2021, 2023, 2026 கிராம சபைகளில் குவாரிக்கு' is an incomplete sentence with no verb, making its meaning unclear
  caption states the 4-acre application was 'அனுமதி கேட்டு விண்ணப்பிக்கப்பட்டது' while the article says the earlier application was for the quarry and a fresh permission request was made, mixing the two applications into one fact
  reel_script omits that the district administration is being accused of submitting a false report to hide the truth, an important point of the article
  reel_script omits that residents were earlier told a sub-division of the land was planned by notice, an important detail of the article
